{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Tied-swift.struct"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether this element marks the start or the stop of the tie."}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"kind","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV4NoteV4TiedV4kindAA12MXLStartStopOvp","symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLStartStopO","text":"MXLStartStop"}]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note\/tied-swift.struct\/kind"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLStartStopO","text":"MXLStartStop","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStop"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"type"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Tied-swift.struct\/kind"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLMetronome","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLMetronome","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"displayed in the music notation."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Note","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Note","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome-note type defines the appearance of a note within a metric relationship mark."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note","title":"MXLMetronome.Note"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStartStop":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstartstop","title":"MXLStartStop","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStartStop","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStartStop"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The start-stop type is used for an attribute of musical elements that can either start or stop, such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tuplets."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStop"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note/Tied-swift.struct":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Tied-swift.struct","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Tied","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Tied","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome-tied indicates the presence of a tie within a metric relationship mark. As with the tied"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element, both the start and stop of the tie should be specified, in this case within separate metronome-note"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note\/tied-swift.struct","title":"MXLMetronome.Note.Tied"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note/Tied-swift.struct/kind":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Tied-swift.struct\/kind","role":"symbol","type":"topic",